270
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:15,800
But I'm nothing like that.

271
00:10:16,270 --> 00:10:18,920
We have absolutely nothing in common.

272
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:21,880
If there's one thing we have in common,
to put it bluntly,

273
00:10:21,880 --> 00:10:23,560
it's this face. Thank you!

274
00:10:24,500 --> 00:10:25,510
Of course.

275
00:10:25,650 --> 00:10:29,160
The similarity between me
and the character

276
00:10:29,410 --> 00:10:31,750
would be our body language

277
00:10:30,890 --> 00:10:32,310
[Posture]

278
00:10:31,910 --> 00:10:35,200
and empathy for others.

279
00:10:32,930 --> 00:10:34,510
[Empathy]

280
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:37,050
The difference may be

281
00:10:37,160 --> 00:10:41,800
that sometimes I have to
act all innocent and clueless.

282
00:10:41,030 --> 00:10:42,120
[Pretending to be innocent and ignorant]

283
00:10:41,800 --> 00:10:44,370
-It's hard to explain.
-Acting careless?

284
00:10:45,350 --> 00:10:47,600
What do you mean?

285
00:10:49,160 --> 00:10:51,550
Maybe it's not too much like me.

286
00:10:51,760 --> 00:10:54,880
-Playing dumb.
-Yes, this is not like me.

287
00:10:55,450 --> 00:10:58,750
I'll say the differences first.
It should be

288
00:10:59,100 --> 00:10:59,920
pulling a long face.

289
00:10:59,100 --> 00:10:59,920
[Pulling a long face]

290
00:11:00,050 --> 00:11:01,630
Actually, I'm not one
to show my displeasure in real life.

291
00:11:01,630 --> 00:11:02,950
I just lose it in private.

292
00:11:02,350 --> 00:11:03,110
[What? What's going on?]

293
00:11:03,110 --> 00:11:05,240
But...

294
00:11:05,240 --> 00:11:08,090
I mean, I just freak out in my head.

295
00:11:08,090 --> 00:11:11,570
In my heart, like, "Oh my, oh my,"
but I won't say it out loud.

296
00:11:11,570 --> 00:11:13,000
However, for Preem,

297
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:14,520
she is the kind of person
who shows it directly.

298
00:11:14,520 --> 00:11:17,170
For example, if she's unhappy
or doesn't like something,

299
00:11:17,170 --> 00:11:19,840
she will say it directly.

300
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:22,570
But in real life,
I don't say everything out loud.

301
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:24,960
I tend to keep things to myself.

302
00:11:25,250 --> 00:11:27,400
Then, if we talk about similarities,

303
00:11:27,400 --> 00:11:28,960
I'd say it's that
when I get some information,

304
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:32,130
I dig deeper and try to make sense of it,

305
00:11:32,130 --> 00:11:37,200
and figure out
how I can use it to my advantage,

306
00:11:37,310 --> 00:11:38,330
before gradually

307
00:11:38,670 --> 00:11:40,880
forming my own opinion and expressing it.

308
00:11:40,880 --> 00:11:44,600
Mueanfan and I are quite different.

309
00:11:44,600 --> 00:11:47,390
She's a little overly fussy and affected,

310
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:47,850
[Sweet and cute]

311
00:11:47,850 --> 00:11:49,720
whether it's the way she dresses,
the way she speaks,

312
00:11:49,720 --> 00:11:52,110
how she acts all cute and clingy,
or even how she asks people for help.

313
00:11:52,110 --> 00:11:55,760
I don't usually dress
in a cute, girly style.

314
00:11:54,400 --> 00:11:55,470
[Not very sweet]

315
00:11:56,070 --> 00:11:57,970
And I'm someone who feels bad
about bothering others

316
00:11:57,530 --> 00:11:58,670
[Embarrassed to bother others]

317
00:11:57,970 --> 00:12:00,440
and finds it hard to ask anyone for help.

318
00:12:00,440 --> 00:12:04,840
So it's a bit hard to play Mueanfan
in this regard.

319
00:12:04,840 --> 00:12:08,920
Why doesn't she care about others?

320
00:12:09,040 --> 00:12:13,050
Namkhing and I are very similar
in personality.

321
00:12:12,490 --> 00:12:13,240
[Very similar]

322
00:12:13,400 --> 00:12:15,490
I hardly need to act.

323
00:12:15,640 --> 00:12:17,920
Because I am the kind
of person who cares about friends

324
00:12:17,920 --> 00:12:20,160
and loves friends very much.

325
00:12:20,160 --> 00:12:22,640
No matter what happens or how busy I am,

326
00:12:22,640 --> 00:12:24,930
I will say, "I'll come to you right now."

327
00:12:25,070 --> 00:12:26,640
[Caring for friends]

328
00:12:25,410 --> 00:12:27,760
This is really very much like me.

329
00:12:27,760 --> 00:12:30,160
And I'm also the kind of person
who has leadership skills

330
00:12:30,160 --> 00:12:32,310
and can give good advice to friends.

331
00:12:32,310 --> 00:12:36,170
So playing her comes naturally to me.
It's 100% me.

332
00:12:36,320 --> 00:12:39,520
Let's move on to the next question.

333
00:12:39,770 --> 00:12:44,520
[How challenging is this role?]

334
00:12:39,770 --> 00:12:42,320
When you have to get
into character to act,

335
00:12:42,530 --> 00:12:46,230
what is the hardest thing for everyone?

336
00:12:46,680 --> 00:12:50,360
For me, the hardest thing
about playing Alice

337
00:12:50,360 --> 00:12:52,850
was being shy.

338
00:12:50,990 --> 00:12:51,720
[Shy]

339
00:12:53,050 --> 00:12:54,680
That was really hard.

340
00:12:54,680 --> 00:12:55,680
Because in real life,

341
00:12:55,680 --> 00:12:57,040
I don't get shy easily.

342
00:12:57,040 --> 00:12:58,560
And even if I do get shy,

343
00:12:58,560 --> 00:13:00,120
I'm good at hiding it.

344
00:13:00,470 --> 00:13:05,470
Or I won't act so flustered.

345
00:13:05,470 --> 00:13:06,800
I have to act natural.

346
00:13:06,970 --> 00:13:10,040
Well, I didn't know
how to find that balance.

347
00:13:10,040 --> 00:13:12,690
I wasn't sure if acting too shy
would look forced

348
00:13:12,690 --> 00:13:16,010
or if I didn't do enough,
the audience might not notice it.

349
00:13:17,040 --> 00:13:20,760
So after every scene
where I needed to be shy,

350
00:13:20,970 --> 00:13:23,040
I'd sit there wondering
if I'd done a good job.

351
00:13:23,040 --> 00:13:27,550
I always felt a little uneasy because I wasn't
confident about portraying shyness.

352
00:13:27,550 --> 00:13:30,160
But please support me.

353
00:13:30,670 --> 00:13:32,530
I really don't get shy very often.

354
00:13:32,850 --> 00:13:36,000
As for playing Nannalin,

355
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:37,840
the hardest part was probably

356
00:13:37,840 --> 00:13:41,830
when she lectured her subordinates
and gave work instructions.

357
00:13:41,830 --> 00:13:43,600
Whenever she spoke,

358
00:13:43,600 --> 00:13:47,100
every word she said exuded confidence.

359
00:13:46,750 --> 00:13:47,800
[Confident]

360
00:13:47,670 --> 00:13:48,880
"I don't think it should be like this."

361
00:13:48,880 --> 00:13:50,590
"That client wants that kind of effect..."

362
00:13:50,590 --> 00:13:52,130
It was really hard.

363
00:13:52,390 --> 00:13:54,800
Because I'm naturally a bit forgetful.

364
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:57,250
Looking at all those packed schedules
and itineraries...

365
00:13:57,250 --> 00:14:00,400
-Nannalin left no time to think.
-Yes.

366
00:14:00,400 --> 00:14:01,870
"They must do this and that."

367
00:14:01,870 --> 00:14:05,200
"Put all the materials
on my desk at the specified time."

368
00:14:05,200 --> 00:14:06,680
It was really very hard.

369
00:14:06,840 --> 00:14:10,360
I also had to clear my mind
and get everything straight.

370
00:14:10,900 --> 00:14:12,160
Keeping track of the lines and
all the scheduling details was really hard.

371
00:14:12,160 --> 00:14:13,560
As for playing Namhom,

372
00:14:13,560 --> 00:14:17,850
the hardest part was

373
00:14:18,170 --> 00:14:19,750
acting cute.

374
00:14:18,910 --> 00:14:19,750
[Cute and naive]

375
00:14:19,750 --> 00:14:22,240
Because normally I really never act cute.

376
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:23,390
That's just not my style at all.

377
00:14:23,390 --> 00:14:27,230
She's kind of cute in an annoying way.

378
00:14:27,600 --> 00:14:29,130
You can ask Alice about it.

379
00:14:30,330 --> 00:14:32,120
-Yes.
-It's to that extent.

380
00:14:32,270 --> 00:14:33,690
"Is this okay?"

381
00:14:34,070 --> 00:14:35,800
"Memorizing lines like this?"

382
00:14:35,930 --> 00:14:36,800
It's just like this.

383
00:14:36,800 --> 00:14:39,600
As for playing Preem, it was the scenes
where I had to give people attitude.

384
00:14:39,600 --> 00:14:41,010
And I had to give attitude to Namhom.

385
00:14:39,600 --> 00:14:41,010
[Short-tempered and capricious]

386
00:14:41,200 --> 00:14:44,200
But actually, I didn't even dare
to look Jinny in the eye.

387
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:47,000
But I had to look her right
in the eye and yell at her.

388
00:14:47,200 --> 00:14:49,160
Actually, I'm a very cute person.

389
00:14:50,430 --> 00:14:51,680
Okay.

390
00:14:51,800 --> 00:14:54,730
You actually acted
the lashing-out part quite well.

391
00:14:54,870 --> 00:14:56,510
You didn't miss a single shot.

392
00:14:56,510 --> 00:14:59,760
As for Mueanfan,
the hardest part was probably,

393
00:15:00,490 --> 00:15:01,920
how should I put it,
that kind of innocence.

394
00:15:01,270 --> 00:15:02,710
[Innocent]

395
00:15:01,920 --> 00:15:05,160
When something should
have made her think twice,

396
00:15:05,160 --> 00:15:06,730
she just didn't give it much thought.

397
00:15:06,730 --> 00:15:09,840
For example, the scenes
where she had to scold Namhom.

398
00:15:09,840 --> 00:15:11,030
Coming from anyone else,

399
00:15:11,030 --> 00:15:14,570
those lines would sound pretty harsh.

400
00:15:14,570 --> 00:15:17,640
But Mueanfan's tone
and actions were

401
00:15:17,640 --> 00:15:20,690
like a child who doesn't feel bad
about saying those things.

402
00:15:20,690 --> 00:15:22,970
I had to perform
those lethal-sounding lines

403
00:15:22,970 --> 00:15:26,520
and deliver them as if she were saying,
"I don't know. I don't even know what I just said."

404
00:15:26,520 --> 00:15:28,610
Just like that.

405
00:15:29,450 --> 00:15:31,930
For playing Namkhing,
the hardest part should be

406
00:15:31,930 --> 00:15:32,880
memorizing her lines, right?

407
00:15:32,590 --> 00:15:33,850
[Memorizing lines]

408
00:15:32,880 --> 00:15:34,130
Because...

409
00:15:34,870 --> 00:15:37,840
Right, the first day
we shot scenes together.

410
00:15:37,840 --> 00:15:39,470
The lines that day were really super long.

411
00:15:39,470 --> 00:15:42,840
-Very long, about two to four pages of lines.
-Two pages, four pages.

412
00:15:42,840 --> 00:15:44,520
It was really too much that day.

413
00:15:44,520 --> 00:15:45,800
That was the hardest part.

414
00:15:45,800 --> 00:15:47,240
As for the acting itself,

415
00:15:47,240 --> 00:15:49,130
like I just said,
she's already very similar to me.

416
00:15:49,130 --> 00:15:50,300
There was no problem with that.

417
00:15:50,300 --> 00:15:51,730
The hardest part was memorizing lines.

418
00:15:51,730 --> 00:15:54,190
-The lines were indeed very long.
-Too long.

419
00:15:54,470 --> 00:15:57,200
When someone asks you to audition,
you're like, "Call me back later.

420
00:15:57,200 --> 00:15:58,000
We'll see."

421
00:15:58,890 --> 00:16:00,770
Okay. The next question is,

422
00:16:00,770 --> 00:16:02,040
is there any scene

423
00:16:01,910 --> 00:16:05,130
[Which scene was the hardest?]

424
00:16:02,040 --> 00:16:04,970
that took more energy
to perform than expected?

425
00:16:05,570 --> 00:16:09,490
If we're talking about that,

426
00:16:09,490 --> 00:16:11,420
there's only this one, which is...

427
00:16:11,450 --> 00:16:12,230
Crying scenes.

428
00:16:12,230 --> 00:16:13,240
-No.
-Oh, no?

429
00:16:13,240 --> 00:16:16,280
-Not crying scenes.
-I was crying throughout the whole show.

430
00:16:16,280 --> 00:16:17,790
I think crying scenes were okay.

431
00:16:17,790 --> 00:16:20,200
The hard part was portraying
that sunny, optimistic outlook

432
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:21,210
[The world is full of sunshine]

433
00:16:20,960 --> 00:16:22,720
where everything is wonderful

434
00:16:22,720 --> 00:16:26,270
and the sky looks like
it's painted in pastel colors.

435
00:16:26,270 --> 00:16:28,830
I'm not that kind of person in real life.

436
00:16:28,830 --> 00:16:31,950
I'm very quiet, even a bit boring,

437
00:16:29,400 --> 00:16:30,760
[Introverted]

438
00:16:32,350 --> 00:16:34,530
and I'm a low-energy person.

439
00:16:34,530 --> 00:16:36,200
But as someone who's naturally quiet,

440
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:39,000
I have to force myself to cheer up
for the role and act like, "Hi! Wow!

441
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:39,800
Is that so?"

442
00:16:39,800 --> 00:16:40,800
things like that.

443
00:16:40,970 --> 00:16:43,450
It really drained my energy.

444
00:16:43,590 --> 00:16:44,960
I had to force myself
to get into the zone.

445
00:16:44,960 --> 00:16:46,800
Once I finished a scene, I could
immediately leave that energy behind

446
00:16:46,800 --> 00:16:48,280
and switch right back to being myself.

447
00:16:48,280 --> 00:16:50,800
This is where it took a lot of energy

448
00:16:50,800 --> 00:16:53,320
for me.

449
00:16:53,470 --> 00:16:54,570
What drained your energy the most?

450
00:16:54,570 --> 00:16:58,040
Every time I played Nannalin,
I felt it drained my energy.

451
00:16:58,160 --> 00:17:01,870
It felt like I was constantly fighting
against the character.

452
00:17:02,300 --> 00:17:04,790
Becoming Nannalin required me
to be pretty cold-hearted.

453
00:17:03,840 --> 00:17:05,069
[A bit aloof]

454
00:17:04,790 --> 00:17:06,650
She's always either snapping at people

455
00:17:06,650 --> 00:17:08,270
or being ice-cold toward them.

456
00:17:06,650 --> 00:17:07,270
[Cold]

457
00:17:08,270 --> 00:17:09,790
It's like she doesn't
have normal human emotions.

458
00:17:09,790 --> 00:17:11,710
Yes, she just doesn't smile.

459
00:17:11,869 --> 00:17:13,690
Sometimes I even complained in my heart,

460
00:17:13,690 --> 00:17:16,069
"Do you have to be this cold?"

461
00:17:16,210 --> 00:17:18,839
I had to calm myself down
and suppress my own emotions,

462
00:17:18,839 --> 00:17:20,900
and bring myself
to a very low emotional state.

463
00:17:20,900 --> 00:17:22,099
Suppose our emotions
are usually at this level。

464
00:17:22,099 --> 00:17:23,950
Playing Nannalin meant pushing it down,

465
00:17:23,950 --> 00:17:27,160
becoming emotionless,
not having too many feelings.

466
00:17:27,300 --> 00:17:28,840
I had to stay completely focused
and maintain that state.

467
00:17:28,840 --> 00:17:31,070
So it really drained my energy.

468
00:17:31,070 --> 00:17:32,010
As for the character Namhom,

469
00:17:32,010 --> 00:17:37,160
it was probably playing
those tense scenes.

470
00:17:35,760 --> 00:17:36,810
[Tense and serious atmosphere]

471
00:17:37,160 --> 00:17:39,360
While delivering her lines, she needed
the entire room to be completely silent.

472
00:17:39,360 --> 00:17:40,760
That was like...

473
00:17:41,100 --> 00:17:43,440
Oh, it was really so nerve-wracking,

474
00:17:43,560 --> 00:17:46,000
so nervous that my armpits
were practically drenched in sweat.

475
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:49,560
-It felt like being enveloped by invisible pressure.
-Yes.

476
00:17:48,690 --> 00:17:49,560
[Feeling under immense pressure]

477
00:17:49,880 --> 00:17:50,890
As for Preem,

478
00:17:50,890 --> 00:17:53,640
it was probably the scenes
where she had to act extremely confident.

479
00:17:53,170 --> 00:17:54,510
[Full of confidence]

480
00:17:53,810 --> 00:17:57,600
I needed to talk about products
or related things
with full confidence,

481
00:17:57,600 --> 00:18:00,040
acting like, "I am confident about this.

482
00:18:00,170 --> 00:18:02,710
I'm going to say it this way,
and no one can refute me."

483
00:18:02,710 --> 00:18:04,810
These emotionally intense scenes

484
00:18:04,810 --> 00:18:08,080
really drained me.

485
00:18:08,830 --> 00:18:10,680
As for Mueanfan, I'd say...

486
00:18:10,680 --> 00:18:12,440
acting opposite Aoom—

487
00:18:12,440 --> 00:18:13,760
the scene where she got scolded by Aoom.

488
00:18:12,960 --> 00:18:13,960
[The scene of being scolded]

489
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:16,230
I really felt like
I was being scolded at that time,

490
00:18:16,230 --> 00:18:17,430
and my tears were about to fall.

491
00:18:17,430 --> 00:18:19,610
And also, how should I put it?

492
00:18:19,610 --> 00:18:22,480
-We had to shoot from different angles.
-Switching camera angles.

493
00:18:22,480 --> 00:18:23,960
So I had to keep going.

494
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:26,730
That day
really took a lot of energy,

495
00:18:26,730 --> 00:18:27,800
plus we started shooting early
in the morning.

496
00:18:27,800 --> 00:18:29,660
So those serious-looking scenes

497
00:18:29,770 --> 00:18:32,440
were quite stressful.

498
00:18:32,970 --> 00:18:34,150
To clarify,

499
00:18:34,510 --> 00:18:36,830
I'm not the mean one. Nannalin is.

500
00:18:36,830 --> 00:18:37,630
I'm not mean.

501
00:18:39,910 --> 00:18:40,680
Okay.

502
00:18:40,680 --> 00:18:41,740
As for Namkhing...

503
00:18:42,070 --> 00:18:44,900
None of my scenes
were particularly exhausting.

504
00:18:45,100 --> 00:18:45,730
Honestly,

505
00:18:45,730 --> 00:18:48,880
Namkhing put energy into every scene,

506
00:18:48,880 --> 00:18:50,800
but not to the point of exhaustion.

507
00:18:50,800 --> 00:18:53,750
Because my character
was responsible

508
00:18:53,750 --> 00:18:55,120
for cheering my friends up,
helping them feel happy again,

509
00:18:55,120 --> 00:18:56,760
and bringing her back to a happy state.

510
00:18:56,760 --> 00:18:58,280
It did take a little energy out of me,

511
00:18:58,280 --> 00:18:59,950
but would I say it takes a lot?

512
00:18:59,950 --> 00:19:01,120
Not really.

513
00:19:01,120 --> 00:19:03,530
It was all pretty manageable overall.

514
00:19:03,700 --> 00:19:06,700
Maybe it's because
you fit the character quite well.

515
00:19:06,910 --> 00:19:09,310
Maybe it's tiring because you're
constantly having to be someone else.

516
00:19:09,310 --> 00:19:10,790
It's not that forced.

517
00:19:10,090 --> 00:19:11,400
[Tired because you can't be yourself]

518
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:13,560
-The process of becoming the character can be a bit hard.
-Right.

519
00:19:13,560 --> 00:19:14,430
Then...

520
00:19:14,570 --> 00:19:15,760
Let's move on to the next question.

521
00:19:15,760 --> 00:19:20,400
[Snap out of character
as soon as "cut" is called]

522
00:19:15,760 --> 00:19:18,640
After shooting heartbreaking scenes,

523
00:19:18,640 --> 00:19:21,760
how do you all get out of character?

524
00:19:21,930 --> 00:19:22,920
I'll answer first.

525
00:19:22,920 --> 00:19:25,470
I don't have
any heartbreaking emotional scenes.

526
00:19:25,470 --> 00:19:26,130
Okay.

527
00:19:26,130 --> 00:19:29,210
Frankly, since I started acting,

528
00:19:29,210 --> 00:19:32,250
I've never had trouble
snapping out of character.

529
00:19:31,010 --> 00:19:32,370
